+    ONE FUNCTION, EVERY ATTACH SITE (2026-08-31). Three flags describe the
+    FAILURE of a previous falsifier: `mechanical_fault` (the instrument did not
+    discriminate), `irreducible_escalation` and `hil_escalated` (the ladder ran
+    out and a human was asked). All three are statements about a specific
+    falsifier. The moment a REPLACEMENT falsifier is attached and the runner
+    itself verifies it, all three describe something that is no longer there.
+
+    THE GAP THIS CLOSES. The 2026-08-31 repair added the `mechanical_fault`
+    clear at the ROUTING success site, beside the two escalation clears already
+    there. It did not reach the POST-CONVERGENCE SWEEP, which is the second
+    place a replacement falsifier is attached and runner-verified:
+
+        e["falsifier_code"] = code
+        e["falsifier_verdict"] = "CONFIRMED"
+        e["verified"] = True
